  "ingredients": [
    "1 teaspoon butter",
    "4 large shallots, peeled and sliced",
    "1 pinch salt",
    "1 cup red wine",
    "2 cups veal stock",
    "salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/gM9pskUagc1bEGfI4NQLgxONNxw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/234930-how-to-make-bordelaise-sauce-ddmfs-Step-1-0041-b73ebb99bb9a46708ae00e25eeed0ea8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234930/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt butter in a saucepan over medium-low heat. Add shallots and a pinch of salt; cook and stir shallots until caramelized and browned, about 20 minutes, stirring occasionally.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/4o6uzWHVD0m7BBe4Fyx7OievOkc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/234930-how-to-make-bordelaise-sauce-ddmfs-step-2-0042-882521745e2f4702b33de5dd0c3c1578.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234930/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add red wine and bring to a simmer. Reduce heat to low; cook until wine is nearly evaporated and pan juices are thick and slightly syrupy. Watch carefully as the mixture burns easily. Add veal stock, return to a simmer, and cook until reduced by half and sauce is slightly thickened, about 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Jo3GPend59z42cdpcowkcBOdkJs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/234930-how-to-make-bordelaise-sauce-ddmfs-step-4-0051-6bf43c19d11e45f48995d444487400b8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234930/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour sauce through a fine mesh strainer set over a container. Tap the strainer with a spoon while straining and squeeze out the last remaining drops of sauce from the residue. Season sauce to taste with salt and black pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/o0UTZPrkA76y0sDM0nhkc6KSL2c=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/234930-how-to-make-bordelaise-sauce-ddmfs-0089-4x3-5d031041edda4278932d8c5203d37800.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234930/step_04.webp"
    }
  ],
